  message: "Bakeoff validation results (deep-20260409-054615, alertmanager + prometheus + kafka):\n\n1. WI-sukav (concrete-extends gate, PR #2817): VALIDATED. Zero spurious InclusiveRange→concrete dispatches_to edges. 3 remaining InclusiveRange edges are legitimate interface→concrete dispatches from stringableRange. Fix confirmed working.\n\n2. WI-kuroj (return-type registry, PR #2824): NOT WORKING. All 708 chained calls in prometheus are unresolved (chained_call_unresolved). Zero edges have return_type metadata. The registry is either not populating for these methods or not being consulted during edge resolution. The promtool→Engine.exec chain remains broken. Needs investigation — reopening INV-dihos or creating a follow-up.\n\n3. INV-bivot (event_publishes traversal): CANNOT VALIDATE on kafka. Kafka implements a message broker but doesn't use application-level event frameworks (Spring @EventListener, JS EventEmitter) internally. The event-sourcing linker found zero patterns. Unit tests provide structural coverage. Need a different repo — something using Spring events or EventEmitter. Side finding: message-queue linker misclassifies Java consumer.subscribe(List.of(...)) as Redis pub/sub."  # 9550
